.TH VDR-SUITE-LOGO-SYNC 1 "October 2026" "VDR-Suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-logo-sync \- synchronize channel logo files into the VDR-Suite cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-logo-sync
.RI [ --source-dir " DIR" " | " --source-url " ZIP-URL" ]
.RI [ --target-dir " DIR" ]
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.br
.B vdr-suite-logo-sync
.B --self-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy supported channel logo images from a local directory or download a ZIP
archive and synchronize its images into the VDR-Suite channel logo cache.
PNG and SVG inputs are accepted; other extensions are ignored.  File names
are normalized for local lookup.  This command does not configure VDR,
install a VDR plugin, or start a VDR-Suite service.
.PP
Without
.BR --source-dir ,
the command fetches an external ZIP archive.  An operator must assess the
source's trust and the logos' licensing/redistribution terms separately.
The daemon can serve files found in its configured channel logo cache.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --source-dir " DIR"
Read a directory tree instead of downloading a ZIP archive.
.TP
.BI --source-url " ZIP-URL"
Archive to fetch if no local source directory was specified.
The default is the 3PO/Senderlogos master ZIP hosted on GitHub.
.TP
.BI --target-dir " DIR"
Cache destination, default
.IR /var/cache/vdr-suite/channel-logos .
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print files that would be copied without creating target files.  If an
archive source is used, the archive is still downloaded for inspection.
.TP
.B --self-test
Execute a local temporary-directory test, then exit without updating the
configured channel-logo cache.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_CHANNEL_LOGO_SYNC_URL
Default source URL when
.B --source-url
is not provided.
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_CHANNEL_LOGO_CACHE
Default target directory when
.B --target-dir
is not provided.
.SH SECURITY
Treat external logo archives as untrusted input and review imported content
and applicable usage rights.  The default target may require administrative
filesystem permissions.  Do not run this helper with elevated privileges
against an untrusted archive without an approved maintenance procedure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
